-- ---- what changed ---------------------------------------------------------
-- The amendment that matters: LIMITS.md still says provenance is never
-- collected, and `retainTicks` collects it. Neither LIMITS.md nor README.md
-- mentions the window; the decision is recorded only in
-- docs/time-and-continuity.md.

amends[map](d_retain_ticks, l_frozen_never_collected).

-- THE TEN RULES, and what their deletion did to the contract. START.md §3.2
-- puts stratification in boot.rofl as data and keeps a checker out of the
-- kernel; `src/rounds.ts` peels the phase order off the decoded rules, so that
-- sentence is not kept as written and `s_no_stratification_checker` is amended
-- rather than qualified — it is CONTRADICTED, not narrowed, and nothing
-- mechanical can hold a sentence that is false.
--
-- `s_reject_unstratified` was written as an amendment here first, and the model
-- refused it: `r_unstratifiable_is_budgeted` already qualifies that duty, and
-- retiring a qualified obligation would have marked a live, tested duty as no
-- longer owed — the flattering direction this ledger's own note warns about,
-- caught by the check that every qualified duty is still live. The kernel does
-- still reject unstratifiable programs, on both evaluators; what changed is the
-- FORM of the diagnostic, which is a narrowing. So it is a qualification, and
-- the others below are qualifications for the same reason: `stratum/2` is still
-- the stock evaluator's input, still read from derived facts, still partial in
-- the same corner, and `test/phase2.test.ts` holds all of it on that path.
amends[map](r_rounds_replace_strata, s_no_stratification_checker).
qualifies[map](r_rounds_replace_strata, s_reject_unstratified).
qualifies[map](r_rounds_replace_strata, s_strata_read_from_facts).
qualifies[map](r_rounds_replace_strata, s_a_stratum_order).
qualifies[map](r_rounds_replace_strata, l_partial_strata).
qualifies[map](r_rounds_replace_strata, l_unchecked_without_boot).
amends[map](d_dep_graph_is_one_tick, s_appendix_dep_edges).
amends[map](d_next_in_body_rejected, s_grammar_temporal).
amends[map](r_conclusion_tense, s_appendix_dep_edges).
amends[map](r_flows_to, s_appendix_leak).
amends[map](r_vocabulary_additions, s_vocabulary_closed).
amends[map](r_stratum_in_kernel_source, s_a_kernel_grep).

-- A QUALIFICATION is not a replacement, and the difference decides whether an
-- obligation still has to be covered. `Facts may be asserted into reserved
-- relations` narrows §2's enforcement without withdrawing it: the rule
-- rejection is still owed and still tested. Filing these three as `amends`
-- would have marked three live, tested obligations as no longer owed, which
-- is the model lying in the flattering direction.
qualifies[map](r_facts_into_reserved, s_reserved_rejected_at_load).
qualifies[map](r_unstratifiable_is_budgeted, s_reject_unstratified).
qualifies[map](r_timeless_kernel_facts, s_persistence_is_a_rule).
qualifies[map](r_edb_for_reserved, l_undefined_silenced_by_one_fact).
qualifies[map](r_moded_relations, l_demand_premise_order).

-- ---- the same obligation, written twice -----------------------------------
-- Seven of the eight prohibited shortcuts in §7 are a §3 or §4 guarantee
-- restated in the negative. The eighth (s7_no_hardcoded_boot) is broader
-- than its §3.2 twin — it covers schema validation and the sees/leak/breach
-- audits as well — so it is not listed here.

restates[map](s7_no_clause_objects, s_evaluator_reads_store).
restates[map](s7_no_log_provenance, s_provenance_per_firing).
restates[map](s7_no_witness_excise, s_excise_not_from_witness).
restates[map](s7_no_nondeterministic_iteration, s_determinism).
restates[map](s7_no_silent_overrun, s_budget_emits_hole).
restates[map](s7_no_skipping_reject_path, s_reject_unstratified).
restates[map](s7_no_pretend_async, s_async_reserved_rejected).

-- ---- obligations discharged by an artefact, not a test --------------------
-- `document the omission` is not testable; it is done or it is not, and the
-- census checks that the document is still there.

discharged_by[map](s_document_no_occurs_check, "LIMITS.md").
discharged_by[map](s_done_readme, "README.md").
discharged_by[map](s_done_limits, "LIMITS.md").
